---
import ColorDots from "../../../../../components/ColorDots/ColorDots.astro";
import SampleWorks from "./SampleWorks/SampleWorks.astro";

const OW_GREEN = "#10AC84";
const OW_GREY = "#676767";
---

<article class="work-item">
  <!-- Project title -->
  <div class="work-title">
    <ColorDots colors={[OW_GREEN, OW_GREY]} />

    <h3>Restaurant Management and POS system</h3>
  </div>

  <!-- Description 1 -->
  <div class="work-description description-left">
    <p>
      It’s not just about adding items, taking orders, and processing payments.
      The system also covers areas like inventory management and accounting,
      which made me realize how much goes on behind a restaurant’s daily
      operations.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Three images -->
  <div class="work-images">
    <img
      src="/images/pexels-valeriya-27969840.jpg"
      alt="Retaurant Menu"
    />
    <img
      src="/images/pexels-imin-technology-276315592-12935045.jpg"
      alt="Order and Pay"
    />
    <img
      src="/images/pexels-bia-limova-1908542654-33175667.jpg"
      alt="Accounting"
    />
  </div>

  <!-- Description 2 -->
  <div class="work-description description-right">
    <p>
      Working on this project taught me that building a good product is more
      than just technical skills like <strong>React</strong>, <strong>TypeScript</strong>, and <b
        >ASP.NET</b
      >. Understanding the business, <b
        >gathering requirements, researching how things work, and asking the
        right questions</b
      > are just as important. These practices helped me better understand the real
      problems behind each feature and design solutions that actually fit the users’
      needs.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Sample works -->
  <SampleWorks />
</article>
